			<div class="content" id="post-content-1362960">
									

<p>Have to confess I browsed over that one far too quickly the first time before realising the interest was the data itself. As such, I like this a lot because it is a nice example of how something quite familiar can be seen as completely alien to, well, something alien. The implication being that some of the more puzzling (or dangerous) SCP may be seen as mundane objects by alternate Foundations, while they would class a Swiss army knife as their equivalent of Euclid.</p>

